    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0562" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/4389: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican, Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-18T16:00:00-05:00">May 18, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Department’s instruction No. 427, May 12. Respectfully suggest that text of
                    proposed note to the Dominican Government enclosed with your instruction be
                    reconsidered in the light of my despatches 3280 April 30, 3287 May 5, and 3300
                    May 9<anchor n="55" xml:id="d400-f1"/> which despatches do not appear to have
                    been before the officers who drafted Department’s instructions.</p>
                <p>I shall defer delivery of proposed note pending Department’s further
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d400-f1" n="55" xml:id="d400-f1-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 3287, May 5, not printed.</p>
